        "name": "DEVINE (wind_downscaling_cnn)",
        "what_it_does": "Fully convolutional U-Net that downscales NWP wind fields to 30m resolution over complex mountain terrain, conditioned on DEM-derived topographic features. Purpose-built for wind-driven snow transport and avalanche-relevant nivology.",
        "how_we_use_it": "Architecture template and potential weight initialization for the terrain downscaling head. Clone the repo, evaluate pretrained weights on Colorado terrain/wind data, and adapt the U-Net architecture for our multi-variable (wind + temperature + precipitation) downscaling head. The closest existing domain match to our target application.",
        "source": "github.com/louisletoumelin/wind_downscaling_cnn + github.com/louisletoumelin/neural_network_and_devine, Zenodo tagged release",
