      {
        "name": "FuXi-CFD",
        "what_it_does": "Generates 3D near-surface wind fields at 30m horizontal resolution from coarse atmospheric inputs plus high-resolution terrain, capturing slope jets, flow deflection, and recirculation that km-scale models average out.",
        "how_we_use_it": "Inference-only evaluation — download the ONNX model from HuggingFace, run it over Colorado avalanche terrain DEMs with HRRR boundary conditions, and use its output as (a) a baseline to beat, (b) potential pseudo-labels for terrain-wind training data generation, and (c) an architecture reference. Cannot fine-tune (ONNX only), but can distill from.",
