        "what_it_does": "IBM/NASA fine-tuned version of Prithvi WxC foundation model for 6x temperature and 8x wind downscaling, validated on MERRA-2, ECCC data, and EURO-CORDEX climate simulations.",
        "how_we_use_it": "Direct comparison baseline — this is the closest existing open-weight model to what we are building (foundation model fine-tuned specifically for weather downscaling). Evaluate it on Colorado stations to establish what a foundation-model-downscaling approach achieves out of the box before investing in custom training.",
        "source": "huggingface.co/ibm-granite/granite-geospatial-wxc-downscaling",
        "pretrained_weights": true
      },
      {
        "name": "SNOWstorm",
        "what_it_does": "Deep-learning emulator (multiple U-Nets) trained on 50m LES that predicts near-surface wind, snow mass change rate, sublimation rate, and snow transport flux — the full wind-driven snow redistribution chain, not just wind.",
        "how_we_use_it": "Evaluate for the wind-loading / snow-redistribution vertical specifically — its output variables (snow mass change, transport flux) map more directly onto avalanche-relevant quantities (windslab loading) than raw wind speed. Investigate whether its intermediate wind-field predictions can serve as initialization or auxiliary targets for our terrain head.",
